quotes = [
    "Top lane: Where champions go to die and never be seen again. In top lane, you spend 10 minutes farming, only to realize that you’re still 1 level behind the enemy jungler who decided your lane was their personal playground. Don't worry, the tower will protect you... until it doesn't.",
    
    "Top lane is the vacuum of League of Legends. You could be playing the most exciting and impactful role in the game... but no, you’re stuck in top lane where it’s just you and a giant minion wave, hoping for a gank that will probably never come.",
    
    "Top lane: The solo queue retirement home. If you want to practice dying alone in silence while your team fights for their lives, top lane is for you. At least mid lane gets roams. Top lane? It gets ignored, then blamed.",
    
    "Top lane is a metaphor for existential dread. You’re alone. You’re irrelevant. You’re behind in gold, behind in levels, and your only interaction with the team is when they ping 'I need help' while you’re stuck in a 1v2 situation. It’s like the game is trying to tell you something… but what?",
    
    "Top lane is the true test of patience. If you love being ignored and wishing that the map would just burn, top lane is your calling. You’ll sit there, push the wave, and wait for your jungler to notice. Spoiler alert: They never do.",
    
    "The only thing worse than playing top lane is being the top laner who thinks they’re important. There’s a reason no one cares about you. You're the forgotten role—existing only to die under a turret or poke at the enemy top laner who just watched a YouTube tutorial on 'How to Make Top Lane Useless.'",
    
    "Top lane is the hole where dreams go to die. You thought you could carry, you thought you had a chance, but then you went top lane. Now you're stuck, no one to help you, and you just want to afk. The best part is when your mid-lane pings you for not being useful. It’s like, ‘I’ve been here the whole time, bro.’",
    
    "Top lane is where impact goes to get reduced to nothing. You’re either getting camped or ignored. When you finally do something useful, it’s either too late or no one noticed. Oh, and don’t even bother with objectives—by the time you get to one, it’s already taken by the enemy jungler.",
    
    "Top lane: The role that proves no one cares until it’s too late. No one asks for help, no one gives you any assistance. You’re expected to be a 1v9 hero who doesn’t have the luxury of roaming or assistance. Good luck with that.",
    
    "Top lane is where champions go to disappear from the map. You can play the most powerful champion in the game, but it doesn’t matter. In top lane, you’re either forced into a passive farm fest, or you’re getting ganked for the 5th time by the enemy jungler, who knows you’re stuck in lane with no escape."
]
